<% title "Fuime Fees" %>

<%# FUIME-DISABLED: `BankFee` is HCB's fiscal-sponsorship fee sweep, not Fuime's
    platform fee.

    Upstream, FeeEngine accrues `event.revenue_fee` into a fee balance, the weekly
    BankFee::WeeklyJob turns each balance into a BankFee, and BankFeeService::ProcessSingle
    settles it with a COLUMN book transfer (`ColumnService.post "/transfers/book"`).
    Fuime has no Column relationship, so that last step cannot run here.

    Under merchant-of-record Fuime's 5% + 50c is taken by Stripe at checkout and posted
    as its own explicit ledger line by Fuime::PaymentWebhookHandler#record_platform_fee.
    FeeEngine::Create then deliberately marks every Fuime-keyed transaction
    `revenue_waived` with a zero amount so the fee is not charged twice, which means a
    Fuime venture never builds a fee balance and never produces a BankFee.

    The view, controller action and model stay on disk (Rule 2: disable, don't delete).
    The admin route is removed, so this is unreachable by URL — the only rows that ever
    landed here came from the pooled-simulator era and are reachable through their
    Fuime Code. Nothing on this page was ever a task.

    ⚠️ `bank_fees_admin_index_path` below no longer exists — the route removal deleted
    the helper. That is harmless only while this template is unreachable: rendering it
    raises NameError. If you restore the route, restore it in config/routes.rb FIRST,
    then the nav items in app/models/admin/nav.rb and app/helpers/static_pages_helper.rb. %>
<%= form_with local: true, class: "card overflow-visible", url: bank_fees_admin_index_path, method: :get do |form| %>
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-2">
    <%= combobox_tag :event_id, event_search_admin_index_path, placeholder: "Event", class: "!max-w-full !min-w-full sm:!min-w-72", value: @event&.to_combobox_display %>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-center mt-2">
    <%= form.submit "Search", class: "ml-auto" %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<div class="flex items-center mb2 flex-col sm:flex-row">
  <div class="flex-grow">
    <%= page_entries_info @bank_fees, entry_name: "Fuime fees" %>
    (<%= render_money @sum %>)
  </div>
  <%= paginate @bank_fees %>
</div>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>ID</th>
      <th>Date</th>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Fuime Code</th>
      <th>Amount</th>
      <th>Event</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @bank_fees.each do |bank_fee| %>
      <%# FUIME: "Memo" and "Actions" removed rather than left blank.

          BankFee has no memo column of its own — the memo lives on the HcbCode, and
          reaching it from here means `HcbCode.find_or_create_by` (BankFee#local_hcb_code),
          i.e. a write per row during a render. The Fuime Code now links to the detail
          page that already shows it.

          "Actions" was empty because there are none: config/routes.rb exposes only
          `get "bank_fees"`, and the one thing that acts on a pending BankFee is
          BankFeeService::ProcessSingle, which posts a Column book transfer. %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= bank_fee.id %></td>
        <td><%= bank_fee.created_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></td>
        <td><%= bank_fee.state_text %></td>
        <td>
          <% if bank_fee.hcb_code.present? %>
            <%= link_to bank_fee.hcb_code, hcb_code_path(bank_fee.hcb_code) %>
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <td><%= render_money bank_fee.amount_cents %></td>
        <td><%= link_to bank_fee.event.name, event_path(bank_fee.event) %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<%= paginate @bank_fees %>
